<div class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-6xl flex-col gap-6">
  <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
    title: "Config",
    subtitle: "Set up your initializer after installation.",
    variant: :h1
  ) %>

  <div class="space-y-3">
    <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
      title: "Steps",
      subtitle: "Follow these steps to configure the gem in your app.",
      variant: :h3,
      class: "mb-0 pb-0"
    ) %>

    <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-6">
      <li>Open <span class="font-mono">config/initializers/recording_studio_ai.rb</span>.</li>
      <li>Paste the initializer template below and adjust values for your environment.</li>
      <li>Add provider API keys and choose the profile/fallback strategy you want to support.</li>
      <li>Restart the app so initializer changes are loaded.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <%= render FlatPack::CodeBlock::Component.new(
    title: "Initializer example",
    language: "ruby",
    code: @config_example
  ) %>

  <div class="space-y-3">
    <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
      title: "Add a Provider",
      subtitle: "How to register providers from a host app or from another gem.",
      variant: :h3,
      class: "mb-0 pb-0"
    ) %>

    <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-6">
      <li>Create a provider class that implements the Recording Studio AI provider contract.</li>
      <li>Register it from the host initializer or in another gem's engine initializer.</li>
      <li>Add the provider to one or more profile candidate lists.</li>
      <li>Optionally enable discovery if your provider class is in the expected providers path.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <%= render FlatPack::CodeBlock::Component.new(
    title: "Provider registration examples",
    language: "ruby",
    code: @provider_extension_example
  ) %>

  <div class="space-y-3">
    <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
      title: "Create Custom Tools",
      subtitle: "Register a tool and call it from generate/stream requests.",
      variant: :h3,
      class: "mb-0 pb-0"
    ) %>

    <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-6">
      <li>Define a stable key and version for your tool.</li>
      <li>Provide clear parameter schema and usage guidance.</li>
      <li>Implement a deterministic executor that returns serializable data.</li>
      <li>Pass the tool reference in the request's custom_tools array.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <%= render FlatPack::CodeBlock::Component.new(
    title: "Custom tool registration and usage",
    language: "ruby",
    code: @custom_tools_example
  ) %>

  <div class="space-y-3">
    <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
      title: "Configuration Reference",
      subtitle: "Meaning, accepted values, and requirement level for each option.",
      variant: :h3,
      class: "mb-0 pb-0"
    ) %>

    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="min-w-full text-left text-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-(--surface-border-color)">
            <th class="px-2 py-2 font-semibold">Key</th>
            <th class="px-2 py-2 font-semibold">Required</th>
            <th class="px-2 py-2 font-semibold">Accepted values</th>
            <th class="px-2 py-2 font-semibold">Explanation</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <% @config_options.each do |option| %>
            <tr class="border-b border-(--surface-border-color)">
              <td class="px-2 py-2 align-top font-mono text-xs"><%= option[:key] %></td>
              <td class="px-2 py-2 align-top"><%= option[:required] %></td>
              <td class="px-2 py-2 align-top"><%= option[:accepted_values] %></td>
              <td class="px-2 py-2 align-top"><%= option[:explanation] %></td>
            </tr>
          <% end %>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
